{
  "sim_type": "excel",
  "title": "NSE Sector Revenue PivotTable — Build the FY25 Cross-Tab",
  "scenario": "You're an analyst at a Mumbai equity-research desk. The NSE has published FY25 sector-quarter revenue numbers for 18 of India's largest listed companies — Reliance, HDFC Bank, TCS, Infosys, ITC, Bajaj Auto, Adani Green, Tata Motors and more. Your PM wants a Sector × Quarter pivot built in five minutes so the team can spot which sectors had the strongest Q4 finish and which lagged. You'll use Excel's native PivotTable UI — drag fields into Rows/Columns/Values, pick aggregations, and read the cross-tab.",
  "instructions": "Use the PivotTable sidebar (right) to BUILD a Sector × Quarter cross-tab of FY25 revenue. Drop SECTOR into ROWS, QUARTER into COLUMNS, REVENUE (₹CR) into VALUES with aggregation SUM. Then verify the four highlighted cell values (Banking-Q1, IT-Q3, FMCG-Q4, Energy-Q2) match the expected ₹Cr figures. Sub-question: switch the VALUES aggregation from SUM to AVERAGE — the screen recomputes live; report Banking-Q1's new value. Bonus filter: drop QUARTER into FILTERS and tick only Q4 — observe how Banking-Q1 disappears.",
  "learning_objective": "Construct a working Sector × Quarter PivotTable in under five minutes by dragging fields into Rows/Columns/Values, switching SUM→AVERAGE aggregations live, and using Filters to narrow the cross-tab.",
  "hints": [
    "PivotTables need three things: a Row field (the dimension running down), a Column field (the dimension running across), and a Value field with an aggregation (the number being summarised). Drag fields from the left sidebar into the four zones.",
    "If you don't see numbers appearing in the grid, your VALUES zone is empty. Drag REVENUE (₹CR) into VALUES — the aggregation defaults to SUM, which is what you want for the first cross-tab.",
    "To switch from SUM to AVERAGE, click the small dropdown next to 'Revenue (₹Cr)' inside the VALUES chip and select AVERAGE — the entire grid recomputes instantly. Same trick for COUNT, MIN, MAX, STDEV."
  ],
